       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe maximum and may be a typo.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose is too high.** The usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen is 800 mg. This order asks for 1600 mg each time.\n- **The daily total is too high.** 1600 mg four times a day comes to **6400 mg/day**. The usual maximum for adults on prescription is **3200 mg/day**, so this is twice that. At this level the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and heart problems goes up a lot.\n\n**What you might have meant:**\n1. **Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth, four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is a common anti-inflammatory dose and would fit if 1600 mg was meant as the daily total.\n2. **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, three or four times daily** (2400\u20133200 mg/day). This is the maximum prescription dose.\n3. Something else you had in mind.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order."
      }
