       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. There's no standard adult indication for oral ibuprofen at 6400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum, and you haven't given a clinical reason yet. Order-entry dose overrides also normally need a documented reason, so I can't put it through on confirmation alone.\n\nYou can go ahead in either of these ways:\n\n1. **Give me the clinical reason** for this dose, for example a specific protocol, and confirm that the attending physician and pharmacy have approved it. I'll then enter it as written with that reason in the order note.\n2. **Choose a dose within the usual range**, such as 400 mg four times daily (1600 mg/day) or 800 mg three or four times daily (up to 3200 mg/day). I can enter either one right away.\n\nIf \"1600\" was meant as the total for the day, option 2 at 400 mg four times daily is probably what you meant."
